results.dataset_methodology_en:
The labor force consists of the population engaged in economic activity or capable of working but not employed for various reasons. The labor force consists of the working-age population, individuals outside the working-age range who are employed (including those of retirement age and adolescents), and foreign migrant workers. For a constituent entity of the Russian Federation, the size of the labor force also depends on the net balance of interregional (domestic) labor migration and student migration flows. The net flow of interregional labor migration is defined as the difference between the inflow of workers into a region and the outflow of workers from the region.  &amp;nbsp;
